WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:04.560
Well, it's official: The latest episode of
The Walking Dead proves that the series is

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.300
downright terrifying again.

00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:10.860
The season nine episode "Bounty" featured
a roughly minute-and-a-half-long sequence

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:13.980
that's one of the most heart-stopping Walking
Dead scenes ever.

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:17.160
Major spoilers ahead, so consider yourself
warned.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:22.820
In 2018, longtime The Walking Dead actor Andrew
Lincoln announced he'd be stepping away from

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:28.420
his post as Rick Grimes, leaving co-star Norman
Reedus to ride his character Daryl Dixon into

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:29.540
"Main Man" territory.

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.460
Many fans of the post-apocalyptic zombie drama
worried the show wouldn't be as exciting without

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:34.960
Rick.

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:36.980
What would The Walking Dead become?

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:42.059
The most recent episode answers that question
for all of us: The Walking Dead would become

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:43.720
absolutely horrifying.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:53.820
On Sunday, February 24th, The Walking Dead
aired the eleventh episode of its ninth season

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:59.019
on AMC, and many viewers hailed one particular
sequence as one of the most genuinely scary

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:01.600
moments The Walking Dead has produced in years.

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:10.180
"I wanted to kill them."

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:15.130
It all starts with Alpha, the leader of The
Whisperers cult, portrayed by Samantha Morton.

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:19.600
At the start of the scene, outside of the
Hilltop settlement, her cronies are holding

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:25.320
two men hostage at knifepoint: Alden and Luke,
portrayed by Callan McAuliffe and Dan Fogler.

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:29.920
Alpha wants to trade these hostages for her
daughter, who's inside of Hilltop.

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:32.820
And just in case that wasn't already tense
enough…

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:41.840
"Hey!"

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:47.660
Shortly thereafter, Alpha instructs the distraught
Whisperer Mother to let the zombies eat her

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:48.160
child:

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:52.760
"If the mother can't quiet the child, then
the dead will.

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:56.300
Natural selection."

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:59.560
And to think we haven't even gotten to the
really scary part yet.

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:04.660
Enter Connie, a Hilltop resident trapped outside
of the gates, who sprints through the surrounding

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:07.580
cornfield and rescues the child… or does
she?

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:16.160
The real horror begins when the sound cuts
out, cleverly mirroring Connie's deafness.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:21.739
As Connie soldiers on, we, the absolutely
terrified viewers, are put in her shoes and

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:23.540
can't see or hear what's around her.

00:02:24.069 --> 00:02:28.360
And just as the undead creeps are within inches
of Connie, Daryl and some other survivors

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:29.540
manage to rescue her.

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:34.719
The scene lasts just over a minute, but it's
undoubtedly one of the smartest and scariest

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:37.260
sequences The Walking Dead has ever produced.

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:41.700
It's a powerful testament to how horrifying
the show can be when it gets creative.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:46.159
Right after the episode aired, The Walking
Dead's Cooper Andrews weighed in on the scene

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:47.540
with some expert analysis:

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:51.440
"Cooper, what does it say about The Whisperers
that they would abandon a baby?"

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:52.560
"They're mean."

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:57.980
Hopefully, The Walking Dead will continue
delivering totally demented sequences throughout

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:02.280
season nine and into season ten, which AMC
ordered in early February.

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:07.140
With the long-running series suffering a diminishing
viewer base in recent years, not to mention

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:12.159
a sharp drop in ratings, showrunners would
be wise to find new ways to ratchet up the

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:12.660
suspense.

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:13.240
Who knows?

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:16.220
Maybe former fans will give The Walking Dead
another go.

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:18.640
Could the show be on the verge of a resurgence?

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:20.940
We're sure AMC would just love that.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:25.740
Fans can find out what new dangers await the
survivors when The Walking Dead returns to

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:28.580
AMC on Sunday, March 3 at 9 PM Eastern Time.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:34.280
In the meantime, we can continue savoring
this one terrifying scene, forever and ever

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:34.780
and ever.

